WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:01.940
This is C. botulinum.

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:04.410
It's a bacterium that can
produce one of the world's

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:06.450
most lethal substances.

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:09.770
It lives in lots of places including soil,

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:13.520
pollen, dust, and also in honey.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:17.203
So why haven't you died from
eating this sweet treat?

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:19.600
Because you're not a baby.

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:26.960
As C. botulinum grows, it
produces botulinum toxin.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:29.501
It's the same stuff used in Botox,

00:00:29.501 --> 00:00:31.426
but Botox has an extremely

00:00:31.426 --> 00:00:34.190
low dose compared to infected food.

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:35.440
In large amounts,

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:37.931
the toxin would attack
your nervous system,

00:00:37.931 --> 00:00:40.460
causing the illness known as botulism,

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:43.780
which can lead to
paralysis and even death.

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:47.360
And since C. botulinum is so
common in our environment,

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:50.240
researchers believe that
bees pick it up on their way

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:52.770
to the hive where they produce honey.

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:55.040
One study found C. botulinum bacteria

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:58.360
in about 8% of honey samples.

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:01.820
But before you purge your
pantry, consider this.

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:05.330
Normally when we encounter
C. Botulinum, like in honey,

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:06.630
it's dormant.

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:10.070
In this sleepy state, it
can't produce the toxin.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.750
Even if you ate it.

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:15.200
Unless, of course, you're
less than 1 year old.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.170
When C. botulinum enters
a baby's large intestine,

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:21.360
it comes alive because
unlike children and adults,

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:24.140
babies less than 1 year
old haven't been eating

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:25.730
real solid foods.

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:27.930
They've been drinking milk.

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:30.480
But when babies are
around 4 to 6 months old,

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:33.340
they stop drinking human
milk, and they start eating

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:36.170
other foods that they've never had before.

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:39.770
As a result, their gut
microbes change very abruptly,

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:42.820
and it's during this transition
period in the baby's gut

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:46.580
that the lethal C. botulinum
bacteria are free to grow

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:48.360
and produce the toxin.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:51.220
As the toxin enters
the baby's bloodstream,

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:54.150
it blocks the ability of
motor nerves to release

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:56.380
acetylcholine, a chemical messenger

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:59.330
that sends nerve signals to muscles.

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:02.650
As a result, the baby starts
to lose control of muscles

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:04.890
and appears tired and floppy.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:07.810
And as more toxin enters
the bloodstream, the muscles

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:11.050
that control swallowing
and breathing stop working.

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:14.190
Fortunately, infant
botulism is not very common,

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:18.130
and infant botulism due
to honey is even rarer.

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:21.741
Fewer than 100 cases
occur in the US each year,

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:24.580
and while it's difficult
to pinpoint the source

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:26.530
of the bacterium in many cases,

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:29.972
experts think that honey accounts for 15%.

00:02:29.972 --> 00:02:33.480
So it's important that if
your infant shows signs

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:35.970
of weakness, you take them to be evaluated

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:38.170
by medical professionals immediately.

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:40.270
In some cases, doctors can administer

00:02:40.270 --> 00:02:42.400
an effective antitoxin,

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:46.140
but it can take babies
weeks or a month to recover.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:49.730
The FDA recommends waiting
until your baby's first birthday

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:52.400
to feed them honey or any products

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:55.413
that are filled with or dipped in honey.

